WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.301
-Welcome back to "Late Night,"
everybody.

00:00:02.301 --> 00:00:03.369
It's been two months since we

00:00:03.369 --> 00:00:04.570
first left the studio

00:00:04.570 --> 00:00:07.239
and we have heard some
of your criticisms

00:00:07.239 --> 00:00:08.574
about our attic shows.

00:00:08.574 --> 00:00:10.943
I want you to know that we
are taking it to heart.

00:00:10.943 --> 00:00:14.447
So, as of today, there will be
no more reference to the copy

00:00:14.447 --> 00:00:16.983
of "The Thorn Birds"
that is on my side table.

00:00:16.983 --> 00:00:19.085
Just gonna be there, but I'm
not gonna talk about it.

00:00:19.085 --> 00:00:21.388
And the number of books
is certainly

00:00:21.388 --> 00:00:23.490
not gonna change
throughout the segment.

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:25.558
Also, I will no longer
be mentioning

00:00:25.558 --> 00:00:27.426
the wasps in my attic,
but that's only because

00:00:27.426 --> 00:00:30.129
we caught the last
two wasps this morning

00:00:30.129 --> 00:00:33.833
and we have trapped them
in that door behind me.

00:00:33.833 --> 00:00:36.202
Now, those are two real wasps

00:00:36.202 --> 00:00:38.638
and not my sons dressed
in homemade wasp costumes,

00:00:38.638 --> 00:00:40.306
who are gonna bust out
when this segment is over,

00:00:40.306 --> 00:00:41.674
so, if you're stickin' around

00:00:41.674 --> 00:00:43.008
for that kind
of adorable content,

00:00:43.008 --> 00:00:46.712
you're wasting your time
because it is not gonna happen.

00:00:46.712 --> 00:00:48.982
Two real wasps, not --
I repeat, not --

00:00:48.982 --> 00:00:51.184
my two boys in wasp costumes

00:00:51.184 --> 00:00:52.986
that I basically spent
the entire weekend makin'

00:00:52.986 --> 00:00:56.055
because I have lost my mind.

00:00:56.055 --> 00:00:57.924
Speaking of lost minds, segue,
the president is

00:00:57.924 --> 00:01:00.927
reeling off fantasies about the
coronavirus just going away

00:01:00.927 --> 00:01:03.596
after two West Wing aides
tested positive

00:01:03.596 --> 00:01:05.598
and unemployment soared
to its highest level

00:01:05.598 --> 00:01:07.400
since the Great Depression.
But don't worry --

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:09.468
he's also trying to distract
from the pandemic

00:01:09.468 --> 00:01:11.437
by obsessing over the
Russia investigation.

00:01:11.437 --> 00:01:14.440
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:01:14.440 --> 00:01:18.011
[ Suspenseful theme plays ]

00:01:18.011 --> 00:01:19.345
It's rarely the case
that someone

00:01:19.345 --> 00:01:21.247
as erratic as Donald Trump
is able to boil

00:01:21.247 --> 00:01:24.751
all the venality, corruption,
and sociopathic incompetence

00:01:24.751 --> 00:01:26.952
of his presidency
down into a single tweet,

00:01:26.952 --> 00:01:29.555
and, yet, over the weekend,
he came pretty close,

00:01:29.555 --> 00:01:32.058
although, in fairness,
he had lots of chances,

00:01:32.058 --> 00:01:33.592
given that, on Sunday, alone,

00:01:33.592 --> 00:01:35.962
he posted 126 tweets
and retweets,

00:01:35.962 --> 00:01:39.231
including over 50 messages
before 8:30 am.

00:01:39.231 --> 00:01:41.400
Sounds like it was
a great Mother's Day.

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:42.702
What did he have for breakfast,

00:01:42.702 --> 00:01:45.738
pancakes covered in Adderall
and 10,000 Diet Cokes?

00:01:45.738 --> 00:01:47.840
[ As Trump ]
Just like Mom used to make.

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:51.210
The president should not have
enough time to tweet that much,

00:01:51.210 --> 00:01:53.913
even on a normal day,
let alone during a crisis

00:01:53.913 --> 00:01:55.248
as nightmarish as this one.

00:01:55.248 --> 00:01:56.749
It's not reassuring.
It's like

00:01:56.749 --> 00:01:58.918
scrolling through your phone
on a flight

00:01:58.918 --> 00:02:00.219
that's going through turbulence

00:02:00.219 --> 00:02:02.855
and seeing your pilot
dancing on TikTok.

00:02:02.855 --> 00:02:04.623
On Sunday, alone,
Trump lashed out

00:02:04.623 --> 00:02:07.460
at everyone from the media
to celebrities, to Democrats;

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:09.528
retweeted random
conspiracy theorists;

00:02:09.528 --> 00:02:10.697
and tried to fabricate

00:02:10.697 --> 00:02:13.032
a totally made-up scandal
called Obamagate.

00:02:13.032 --> 00:02:15.034
Even for Trump,
this was an especially

00:02:15.034 --> 00:02:17.670
demented weekend on Twitter,
and that's saying a lot,

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:19.639
for a guy whose tweets,
generally speaking,

00:02:19.639 --> 00:02:21.340
would make more sense
written backwards

00:02:21.340 --> 00:02:24.243
on the door of a hotel room,
"Shining"-style.

00:02:24.243 --> 00:02:26.712
And, as the U.S. death toll
from the coronavirus climbed

00:02:26.712 --> 00:02:28.147
to nearly 80,000,

00:02:28.147 --> 00:02:30.583
with unemployment at its worst
since the Great Depression,

00:02:30.583 --> 00:02:33.453
Trump chose to take time
out of his day

00:02:33.453 --> 00:02:35.355
to tweet about his own golf club

00:02:35.355 --> 00:02:38.925
and use it as an excuse to both
advertise his personal business

00:02:38.925 --> 00:02:42.595
and parrot his message that
the economy is ready to reopen.

00:02:42.595 --> 00:02:44.764
Trump's golf course
in L.A. announced

00:02:44.764 --> 00:02:46.733
that they were reopening
with a tweet that said,

00:02:46.733 --> 00:02:48.034
"Game on!

00:02:48.034 --> 00:02:49.235
We are thrilled
to announce the reopening

00:02:49.235 --> 00:02:51.737
of @trumpgolfla
beginning Saturday May 9th!

00:02:51.737 --> 00:02:53.506
We look forward
to welcoming you back

00:02:53.506 --> 00:02:55.074
Book your tee time now!"

00:02:55.074 --> 00:02:57.076
And then, Trump retweeted
it and wrote,

00:02:57.076 --> 00:03:00.112
So great to see our Country
starting to open up again!"

00:03:00.112 --> 00:03:02.314
Cool. I'm sure
the 20 million Americans

00:03:02.314 --> 00:03:04.384
who lost their job in April
are stoked to hit the links.

00:03:04.384 --> 00:03:06.885
"Honey, good news --
the unemployment check came.

00:03:06.885 --> 00:03:08.054
Now, I can afford to play

00:03:08.054 --> 00:03:10.022
three and a half holes
at Trump's golf course."

00:03:10.022 --> 00:03:12.525
So, Trump actually found a way
to use a pandemic

00:03:12.525 --> 00:03:14.927
to advertise
his luxury golf resort.

00:03:14.927 --> 00:03:17.230
Reminds me of that time
during the Great Depression

00:03:17.230 --> 00:03:20.266
when FDR advertised
his bindle-making business.

00:03:20.266 --> 00:03:21.934
[ as FDR ]
Are you a hobo looking
for a sack

00:03:21.934 --> 00:03:23.235
to carry your can of beans

00:03:23.235 --> 00:03:25.104
as you ride the rails
in search of work?

00:03:25.104 --> 00:03:27.807
Well, come on down
to FDR's House of Bindles.

00:03:27.807 --> 00:03:29.642
The only thing
we have to fear is

00:03:29.642 --> 00:03:31.778
these crazy-low prices.

00:03:31.778 --> 00:03:35.415
No research went into figuring
out if he sounds like that.

00:03:35.415 --> 00:03:37.883
Anywhere between 1,000
and 2,000 Americans

00:03:37.883 --> 00:03:40.286
are dying every day
from the coronavirus

00:03:40.286 --> 00:03:42.454
and, yet, rather
than confront that reality,

00:03:42.454 --> 00:03:44.223
Trump is doing
the only thing he knows,

00:03:44.223 --> 00:03:46.559
and that's lying
his way through it.

00:03:46.559 --> 00:03:49.195
He's trying to dead-eye
mind-trick Americans

00:03:49.195 --> 00:03:51.964
into thinking coronavirus
will simply go away.

00:03:51.964 --> 00:03:53.799
On Friday, he told reporters
that the coronavirus

00:03:53.799 --> 00:03:56.435
would soon disappear,
even without a vaccine.

00:03:56.435 --> 00:03:58.471
-This is gonna go away
without a vaccine.

00:03:58.471 --> 00:04:01.340
It's gonna go away and it's --
we're not gonna see it again,

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:02.908
hopefully,
after a period of time.

00:04:02.908 --> 00:04:05.811
You may have some --
some flare-ups and,

00:04:05.811 --> 00:04:07.779
I guess, you know,
I would expect that.

00:04:07.779 --> 00:04:12.151
Sometime in the fall,
you'll have flare-ups, maybe.

00:04:12.151 --> 00:04:14.787
Maybe not, but, according
to what a lotta people say,

00:04:14.787 --> 00:04:15.855
you probably will.

00:04:15.855 --> 00:04:17.656
We'll be able to put them out.

00:04:17.656 --> 00:04:19.525
You may have
some flare-ups next year,

00:04:19.525 --> 00:04:21.126
but, eventually,
it's gonna be gone.

00:04:21.126 --> 00:04:22.595
It's gonna be gone.
You know, there are

00:04:22.595 --> 00:04:26.232
some viruses and flus that came
and they went for a vaccine.

00:04:26.232 --> 00:04:28.901
They never found the vaccine
and they disappeared.

00:04:28.901 --> 00:04:30.303
They've never shown up again,

00:04:30.303 --> 00:04:32.438
They die,
too, like everything else.

00:04:32.438 --> 00:04:33.606
They die, too.

00:04:33.606 --> 00:04:34.807
-Holy [bleep]

00:04:34.807 --> 00:04:36.942
Your strategy for dealing
with coronavirus is,

00:04:36.942 --> 00:04:39.178
"Eventually, everything dies"?

00:04:39.178 --> 00:04:40.546
Are you responding to a pandemic

00:04:40.546 --> 00:04:43.015
or narrating
a Werner Herzog movie?

00:04:43.015 --> 00:04:44.617
[ as Herzog ]
Time is nature's

00:04:44.617 --> 00:04:46.152
cruelest weapon.

00:04:46.152 --> 00:04:48.120
Ze clock is an assassin

00:04:48.120 --> 00:04:51.123
silently stalking us
to ze grave

00:04:51.123 --> 00:04:52.724
with his sinister laugh --

00:04:52.724 --> 00:04:55.561
tick-tock, tick-tock.

00:04:55.561 --> 00:04:59.531
I guarantee you Werner
is crushing stay-at-home.

00:04:59.531 --> 00:05:02.635
No one thinks coronavirus
will just go away,

00:05:02.635 --> 00:05:04.036
let alone without a vaccine.

00:05:04.036 --> 00:05:05.538
You already tried
this bull[bleep]

00:05:05.538 --> 00:05:06.773
before this pandemic started

00:05:06.773 --> 00:05:08.307
and it didn't work
back then, either.

00:05:08.307 --> 00:05:09.708
-The virus.

00:05:09.708 --> 00:05:11.277
They're working hard.

00:05:11.277 --> 00:05:13.145
Looks like, by April,
you know, in theory,

00:05:13.145 --> 00:05:16.115
when it gets a little warmer,
it miraculously goes away.

00:05:16.115 --> 00:05:17.216
[ Chuckling ]
I hope that's true.

00:05:17.216 --> 00:05:18.351
Now, the virus

00:05:18.351 --> 00:05:20.886
that we're talkin'
about having to do,

00:05:20.886 --> 00:05:23.456
you know, a lotta people think
that goes away in April

00:05:23.456 --> 00:05:25.858
with the heat,
as the heat comes in.

00:05:25.858 --> 00:05:27.660
Typically,
that will go away in April.

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:29.628
-Nailed it again, Dr. Science!

00:05:29.628 --> 00:05:30.930
Not only is the virus
still here,

00:05:30.930 --> 00:05:32.665
it didn't even get warm yet.

00:05:32.665 --> 00:05:34.666
On that note,
[bleep] off, April.

00:05:34.666 --> 00:05:36.268
What was that?!

00:05:36.268 --> 00:05:37.403
This year of all years.

00:05:37.403 --> 00:05:40.339
Who told you coronavirus
goes away in April?

00:05:40.339 --> 00:05:42.174
Are you confusing it
with March Madness?

00:05:42.174 --> 00:05:43.976
[ As Trump ]
The madness spreads
to basketball courts

00:05:43.976 --> 00:05:45.644
and college campuses
across the country,

00:05:45.644 --> 00:05:47.379
but don't worry.
It goes away in April,

00:05:47.379 --> 00:05:49.848
when either Duke
or Villanova beats it.

00:05:49.848 --> 00:05:51.817
Trump is selling
yet another unhinged fantasy

00:05:51.817 --> 00:05:53.352
to try to coax people
out of their homes

00:05:53.352 --> 00:05:54.587
and back into the economy

00:05:54.587 --> 00:05:57.256
after two West Wing aides
tested for coronavirus

00:05:57.256 --> 00:05:58.557
and The Washington Post reported

00:05:58.557 --> 00:06:00.660
that all White House staffers
received a memo

00:06:00.660 --> 00:06:02.695
from the White House
Management Office on Friday

00:06:02.695 --> 00:06:06.098
which encouraged employees
to practice maximum telework

00:06:06.098 --> 00:06:08.367
and to work remotely,
if at all possible.

00:06:08.367 --> 00:06:10.503
Well, that's easy for Trump,

00:06:10.503 --> 00:06:13.205
since he's already spent
the last three years teleworking

00:06:13.205 --> 00:06:14.240
from his home office

00:06:14.240 --> 00:06:16.576
on the 18th green at Mar-a-Lago.

00:06:16.576 --> 00:06:18.111
Every time you see him
in the Oval Office,

00:06:18.111 --> 00:06:20.245
that's just his Zoom background.

00:06:20.245 --> 00:06:22.447
Think about that --
the president is telling people

00:06:22.447 --> 00:06:23.782
to get back into the workforce,

00:06:23.782 --> 00:06:26.585
while his own White House
tells employees to stay home.

00:06:26.585 --> 00:06:28.187
One day, he's gonna call
a press conference

00:06:28.187 --> 00:06:30.822
to reassure us that
murder hornets are fake news,

00:06:30.822 --> 00:06:33.058
while a dozen of them
carry him back to their nest.

00:06:33.058 --> 00:06:35.060
[ Buzzing ]
"You live with us now, Donald."

00:06:35.060 --> 00:06:37.062
And don't let mention
of the murder hornets

00:06:37.062 --> 00:06:39.965
get you to thinkin' that my kids
are in that door back there,

00:06:39.965 --> 00:06:41.767
dressed like wasps,
'cause they're not,

00:06:41.767 --> 00:06:44.103
and they're not gonna just
barge out at the end

00:06:44.103 --> 00:06:45.537
of this "Closer" --
I'll prove it.

00:06:45.537 --> 00:06:46.939
I'll prove they're not there.
Who wants ice cream?

00:06:46.939 --> 00:06:49.007
They're not there, guys.
They're not there.

00:06:49.007 --> 00:06:51.143
And, by the way,
you'll never guess

00:06:51.143 --> 00:06:52.744
how Trump reacted to the news

00:06:52.744 --> 00:06:55.181
that one of his staffers
had tested positive

00:06:55.181 --> 00:06:57.849
for the virus
he failed to contain.

00:06:57.849 --> 00:07:00.519
After learning that one
of his valets was infected,

00:07:00.519 --> 00:07:02.722
Trump became lava-level mad
at his staff

00:07:02.722 --> 00:07:05.891
and said he doesn't feel it's
doing all it can to protect him.

00:07:05.891 --> 00:07:07.359
First of all, look at 'im.
He's always

00:07:07.359 --> 00:07:08.661
lava-level something.

00:07:08.661 --> 00:07:11.864
If he's not lava-level mad,
he's lava-level happy,

00:07:11.864 --> 00:07:13.699
or, more often than not,
lava-level indifferent.

00:07:13.699 --> 00:07:16.669
Second, Trump is actually upset

00:07:16.669 --> 00:07:18.236
that the people who are
supposed to protect him

00:07:18.236 --> 00:07:19.271
are doing a good job.

00:07:19.271 --> 00:07:20.406
Oh, the irony.

00:07:20.406 --> 00:07:22.674
If we were living
in a story or a fable,

00:07:22.674 --> 00:07:24.744
this would be the moment
where the mean old miser

00:07:24.744 --> 00:07:27.112
finally has a change of heart
and throws money at some kid

00:07:27.112 --> 00:07:29.014
to go buy a goose [ Laughing ]
for the festival or something.

00:07:29.014 --> 00:07:30.115
But this is Donald Trump.

00:07:30.115 --> 00:07:31.250
There's
no change of heart.

00:07:31.250 --> 00:07:32.752
There's no learning curve.

00:07:32.752 --> 00:07:34.986
If this was a Choose
Your Own Adventure story,

00:07:34.986 --> 00:07:36.388
the bottom of every page
would say,

00:07:36.388 --> 00:07:39.425
"Unh, just --
just go to the next page."

00:07:39.425 --> 00:07:42.194
The president is just
profoundly incapable

00:07:42.194 --> 00:07:44.163
of thinking about anyone
other than himself.

00:07:44.163 --> 00:07:46.632
That much has been clear
from day one of this crisis

00:07:46.632 --> 00:07:49.501
and it was on full display
when he called in

00:07:49.501 --> 00:07:51.337
for his latest
teletherapy session

00:07:51.337 --> 00:07:53.072
with the Fox &amp; Friends
on Friday.

00:07:53.072 --> 00:07:54.740
This was the day
the government announced

00:07:54.740 --> 00:07:56.742
truly catastrophic
unemployment numbers

00:07:56.742 --> 00:07:59.578
and the coronavirus death toll
climbed toward 80,000

00:07:59.578 --> 00:08:01.914
and, yet, the president
rambled for 20 minutes

00:08:01.914 --> 00:08:04.649
about God knows what before he
even talked about coronavirus,

00:08:04.649 --> 00:08:05.918
and that was only because

00:08:05.918 --> 00:08:08.287
the Fox &amp; Friends
finally asked him about it.

00:08:08.287 --> 00:08:10.189
-Mr. President,
good morning to ya.

00:08:10.189 --> 00:08:11.624
-Good morning.
-Hi, Steve.

00:08:11.624 --> 00:08:13.525
They know it was just
a total hoax.

00:08:13.525 --> 00:08:17.196
It was a made-up story,
a disgrace to our nation.

00:08:17.196 --> 00:08:20.199
These are dirty politicians
and -- and dirty cops.

00:08:20.199 --> 00:08:23.435
So, Schiff is a crooked
politician, crooked as can be,

00:08:23.435 --> 00:08:25.037
probably one of the worst
I've ever seen.

00:08:25.037 --> 00:08:26.472
I've seen some beauties.

00:08:26.472 --> 00:08:28.273
It was like they just sat there.

00:08:28.273 --> 00:08:29.641
They sat in an office.

00:08:29.641 --> 00:08:31.176
"Hello. Goodbye."

00:08:31.176 --> 00:08:32.177
That would be a meeting.

00:08:32.177 --> 00:08:33.312
"Hello. Goodbye."

00:08:33.312 --> 00:08:36.482
You look at Mueller,
that was purely corrupt.

00:08:36.482 --> 00:08:38.483
And can you imagine,
with all the corruption

00:08:38.483 --> 00:08:39.852
having to do with Mueller,

00:08:39.852 --> 00:08:42.921
you don't have Clapper;
and Brennan, who's sleaze;

00:08:42.921 --> 00:08:44.623
and a guy like Comey,

00:08:44.623 --> 00:08:45.625
who's a sick man.
-Right.

00:08:45.625 --> 00:08:46.992
I mean, Comey's a sick man.

00:08:46.992 --> 00:08:48.727
He's just a stupid guy.
-Well --

00:08:48.727 --> 00:08:51.730
-He's dumb as a rock
and he's a sick guy.

00:08:51.730 --> 00:08:53.065
There's something wrong
with him.

00:08:53.065 --> 00:08:54.599
We've rebuilt our military.

00:08:54.599 --> 00:08:56.268
This is not what
they love to hear.

00:08:56.268 --> 00:08:58.971
Jeff Sessions was a disaster.

00:08:58.971 --> 00:09:01.940
Well, Kislyak had dinner
with Nancy Pelosi and Schumer,

00:09:01.940 --> 00:09:03.242
all these guys, they all,

00:09:03.242 --> 00:09:04.977
everybody in Washington
knew Kislyak.

00:09:04.977 --> 00:09:07.046
But I learned a lot
from Richard Nixon --

00:09:07.046 --> 00:09:08.246
Don't fire people.

00:09:08.246 --> 00:09:11.116
I learned a lot.
I study history.

00:09:11.116 --> 00:09:12.250
If you did a poll there,

00:09:12.250 --> 00:09:13.752
[ Laughing ]
I'd do very well in the FBI.

00:09:13.752 --> 00:09:15.954
But the top was crooked.

00:09:15.954 --> 00:09:17.289
They were dirty cops.

00:09:17.289 --> 00:09:18.958
-Someone get grandpa
off the phone.

00:09:18.958 --> 00:09:20.793
Every time Trump calls in
for one of these,

00:09:20.793 --> 00:09:22.060
we can only see
the "Fox &amp; Friends"

00:09:22.060 --> 00:09:23.662
sittin' there, blinkin',
like a family

00:09:23.662 --> 00:09:26.332
who accidentally bought tickets
to the wrong movie.

00:09:26.332 --> 00:09:27.799
[ Whispering ]
"Does this whole thing
have subtitles?

